# Getting Started

SIBL is a fast, lightweight, zero-dependency static and dynamic linker written in Zig 0.17.0.

It parses ELF, PE/COFF, Mach-O, and static archives with a zero-copy design, resolves symbols, lays out sections and segments, and applies relocations. Binary emission is the next major phase.

## Requirements

- Zig 0.17.0

## Building

```sh
git clone https://github.com/zig-foundry/sibl.git
cd sibl
zig build
```

This produces the `sibl` executable in `zig-out/bin/`.

```sh
zig build run -- --help
zig build test
```

## Quick Test

Compile a minimal object file and inspect it:

```sh
# Create a tiny hello.zig
echo 'export fn main() void {}' > hello.zig
zig build-obj hello.zig -femit-bin=hello.o

# Inspect symbols, sections, and segments
./zig-out/bin/sibl hello.o
```

Expected output includes resolved symbols, a section layout (virtual addresses from `0x400000`), and a segment list with `filesz` / `memsz`.

## Using SIBL as a Library

Add SIBL as a dependency and import the root module:

```zig
const sibl = @import("sibl");

var table = sibl.SymbolTable.init(allocator);
defer table.deinit();

var layout = sibl.Layout.init(allocator, 0x400000, 4096);
defer layout.deinit();
```

Public types are re-exported from `src/root.zig`.

You can also generate HTML documentation for the public API:

```sh
zig build-lib src/root.zig -femit-docs
```

## Project Layout

```
src/
├── alloc.zig     Phase 1.2  — arena and scratch allocators
├── args.zig      Phase 1.3  — CLI argument parser
├── target.zig    Phase 1.4  — target detection and page size
├── file.zig      Phase 1.5  — memory-mapped file reader
├── elf.zig       Phase 2    — ELF parsing
├── strtab.zig    Phase 2.4  — string table reader and builder
├── coff.zig      Phase 3    — PE/COFF parsing
├── macho.zig     Phase 4    — Mach-O parsing
├── archive.zig   Phase 5    — static archive (.a / .lib) parsing
├── symbol.zig    Phase 6    — global symbol table and resolution
├── layout.zig    Phase 7    — section grouping, segments, size accounting
├── reloc.zig     Phase 8    — relocation engine (x86_64, AArch64)
├── root.zig      Public re-exports
└── main.zig      Linker executable entry point
```

See the [Roadmap](https://github.com/zig-foundry/sibl/blob/main/ROADMAP.md) for the full phase plan.

## Next Steps

- Explore the source in `src/`.
- Run the test suite with `zig build test`.
- Follow the roadmap for upcoming phases (entry points, linker scripts, and binary emission).
